+## Core review questions
+
+### 1. Six model options and consent behavior
+
+All six model identifiers (`tiny`, `base`, `small`, `medium`, `large`, `large-v3-turbo`) remain defined in [`_MODELS`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L94-L97) and mapped to their Systran / Mobius Labs Hugging Face repositories in [`_MODEL_REPOSITORIES`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L148-L155). Unknown model inputs safely normalize to `base` via [`normalize_model`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L100-L105).
+
+Explicit consent enforcement is intact. In [`_prepare_model_snapshot`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L243-L261), missing or structurally incomplete cache snapshots raise `PermissionError` when `consent_given=False`. The download helper [`_download_model_snapshot`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L237-L240) executes only after verifying explicit opt-in, followed by structural verification via [`_checked_model_snapshot`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L179-L199).
+
+### 2. Cache resolution and asset acquisition
+
+Cache resolution cannot unexpectedly acquire assets or reach external networks without consent. [`is_model_downloaded`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L221-L228) and [`_cached_model_snapshot`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L201-L219) perform purely read-only checks: they read `refs/main`, inspect directory structure, verify that all three required files (`model.bin`, `config.json`, `tokenizer.json`) exist with non-zero size, and ensure targets stay strictly within the repository root. When unconsented, no directories are created and no download helpers are invoked.
+
+During execution in [`transcribe_audio`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L382-L490), the resolved snapshot path string is passed directly to `whisperx.load_model` along with `local_files_only=True`. Because the passed target is a local directory, faster-whisper selects its existing local directory branch (`elif os.path.isdir(model_size_or_path)`), bypassing its internal `download_model` path.
+
+### 3. Companion delta: tokenizer preparation and non-local fallback
+
+The companion delta in [companion-B.patch.txt](file:///E:/AI/projects/uoink/checkouts/Yoink-library/_scratch/companion-b-static-qualification01/original-proposal01/companion-B.patch.txt) correctly reorders tokenizer preparation ahead of native model instantiation:
+
+- In-memory `tokenizer_bytes` or on-disk `tokenizer_file` are parsed before calling `ctranslate2.models.Whisper`. If the file or buffer is malformed, failure occurs prior to native model allocation.
+- When `local_files_only=True` and no local tokenizer exists, lines 695–696 raise `FileNotFoundError("Local Whisper snapshot is missing tokenizer.json")` before model construction, eliminating the silent fallthrough to remote retrieval.
+- When `local_files_only=False` and the local file is absent, `prepared_tokenizer` remains `None`. CTranslate2 initializes normally, and the existing multilingual-aware fallback `tokenizers.Tokenizer.from_pretrained("openai/whisper-tiny" + ("" if self.model.is_multilingual else ".en"))` executes at lines 712–714.
+
+In the isolated synthetic harness ([constructor-contracts.py.txt](file:///E:/AI/projects/uoink/checkouts/Yoink-library/_scratch/companion-b-static-qualification01/constructor-contracts.py.txt)), the baseline source failed 5 of 6 contracts due to inverted construction order and missing `FileNotFoundError`. The proposed candidate passed all 6 contracts with zero errors. Neither run loaded heavy dependencies or executed a native model constructor.
+
+## Actionable findings
+
+### Finding 1: Empty in-memory tokenizer buffer bypasses buffer loading
+
+- **Call sequence:** A caller invokes `WhisperModel(model_path, files={"tokenizer.json": b""}, local_files_only=True)`.
+- **Consequence:** In Python, `bool(b"")` evaluates to `False`. The check `if tokenizer_bytes:` at line 691 of [companion-B.py.txt](file:///E:/AI/projects/uoink/checkouts/Yoink-library/_scratch/companion-b-static-qualification01/original-proposal01/companion-B.py.txt#L691) treats empty bytes as absent. It falls through to `elif os.path.isfile(tokenizer_file):`. If an ambient file exists at `model_path/tokenizer.json`, it loads the disk file instead of the caller's buffer. If no file exists, it raises `FileNotFoundError` claiming the local snapshot file is missing, rather than reporting an invalid buffer.
+- **Affected lines:** [companion-B.py.txt](file:///E:/AI/projects/uoink/checkouts/Yoink-library/_scratch/companion-b-static-qualification01/original-proposal01/companion-B.py.txt#L691-L696) lines 691–696 (and [companion-B.patch.txt](file:///E:/AI/projects/uoink/checkouts/Yoink-library/_scratch/companion-b-static-qualification01/original-proposal01/companion-B.patch.txt#L9) line 9).
+- **Smallest repair:** Replace `if tokenizer_bytes:` with `if tokenizer_bytes is not None:` so supplied buffers always route to `from_buffer`.
+
+### Finding 2: Identity check on Windows paths risks spurious download verification failure
+
+- **Call sequence:** `_prepare_model_snapshot` calls `_download_model_snapshot`, returning a `Path` from `huggingface_hub.snapshot_download`. The path is passed to `_checked_model_snapshot(data_root, model_size, snapshot)`.
+- **Consequence:** Line 187 of [whisper_runner.py](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L187) tests `snapshot.resolve(strict=True) != snapshot`. On Windows, `snapshot = Path(snapshot).absolute()` retains the caller's input casing (e.g. lowercase drive `c:\`), while `resolve(strict=True)` normalizes drive letters to uppercase and resolves 8.3 short paths. If casing differs, the inequality evaluates to `True`, `_checked_model_snapshot` returns `None`, and line 257 raises a spurious `RuntimeError` claiming the download failed to provide required files.
+- **Affected lines:** [whisper_runner.py](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L184-L188) lines 184 and 187.
+- **Smallest repair:** Normalize `snapshot = Path(snapshot).resolve(strict=True)` first, verify `snapshot.parent == (repo / "snapshots").resolve()`, and check `not snapshot.is_symlink()`.
+
+### Finding 3: Runtime local-only guarantee depends on unmerged Companion B
+
+- **Call sequence:** In the current runtime without Companion B applied, `transcribe_audio` calls `whisperx.load_model(..., local_files_only=True)`. A file replacement or deletion of `tokenizer.json` occurs after `_checked_model_snapshot` succeeds.
+- **Consequence:** Unpatched `faster_whisper.WhisperModel.__init__` allocates the CTranslate2 model, discovers `tokenizer.json` is missing on disk, and falls through to `tokenizers.Tokenizer.from_pretrained(...)`. Because unpatched faster-whisper does not forward `local_files_only` to `from_pretrained`, it initiates an unconsented remote network request to Hugging Face Hub, contradicting the local-only enforcement claim.
+- **Affected lines:** [whisper_runner.py](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/131e52c7-b6e/gemini/whisper_runner.py#L433-L436) lines 433–436 vs unpatched `faster_whisper/transcribe.py` lines 700–708.
+- **Smallest repair:** Qualify and apply Companion B to the staged faster-whisper runtime so missing tokenizers raise `FileNotFoundError` before model allocation and block remote fallback.
+
+## Open scope and verdict
+
+Product A's cache consent repair in commit `b96dbd0` satisfies its stated structural boundary: it passed 144 cases and 13 subtests independently in worker and checkout environments. Companion B's inert proposal in candidate01 resolved all 5 baseline constructor contract failures.
+
+Neither change constitutes an artifact manifest, cryptographic checkpoint validation, or protection against post-check filesystem modification races. Unrestricted default VAD loading and full model-stack runtime qualification remain open scope. This source review approves the bounded logic and contracts as sound, but does not grant release or market approval.
